{
  "format": "call-of-slop-construct-blueprint/1",
  "name": "Haywain Hauler",
  "description": "A medium hauler for the farmers, in a combine harvester's clothes: blocky barn-red cladding, a cream stripe band, a dark chassis. A glass cab room stands out on the nose with a walkway round it, a ladder up to each side and an airlock off each, between the cab room and the crew block; then the crew block (bunks, a head, a galley, an airlock over the boarding shaft); then six standard 2 m containers, two across and three along, in a bay open to the sky inside a raised tank coaming, so a dock's crane lifts each one straight out; then the engine box with its exhaust stacks, and a drive pod slung low on each side. Lift jets and legs under it set it down; attitude jets at both ends and on the pods' noses move it about.",
